This is a prospective Notes candidate, stored only in work/. Production runtime, tests, documentation, registries and earlier receipts stay unchanged. The installed28-file source epoch and31 inert original Joplin source/provenance files were authenticated and copied before coding. The frozen149-artifact current-layout138 acceptance evidence was strictly authenticated; only its exact authority receipts/manifest are copied here, with prior historical stage references retained.

Notebook Trash and Restore now open an actual in-page alert dialog. The visible text names the selected notebook, recursive subnotebook/note scope, retained attachments and the Restore inclusion of separately trashed notes. Confirm and Cancel are real buttons. Cancel receives initial focus; Escape cancels an unanswered question. Tab and reverse Tab cycle the two choices. Background Notes children preserve their prior inert value and become inert while pending. After Confirm both buttons disable, the dialog receives focus and a pending label, and duplicate controls do not issue another request. Backend revisions, recursive changes and saved-draft policy are unchanged. Native browser dialogs remain for other existing actions.

The existing organization busy gate spans confirmation and the real backend request. Cancel returns without notebook mutation or follow-up reads. The request captures notebook ID and organization revision before awaiting the decision. Returning render cleanup cancels an unsubmitted question and ignores retained old buttons. Closing after a committed held response suppresses its old notebook view/status/read publication; it does not undo the commit. The existing app shell already calls this cleanup on replacement. Existing client/markdown routes suffice, so no shared-host change is proposed. This narrow disposal check does not certify every unrelated asynchronous action in the Notes client.

The first fresh9 model campaign passed, with exact source/raw observations retained. Before formal acceptance, a narrow adjustment explicitly focuses the pending dialog after disabling its buttons; current acceptance belongs to the subsequent68 selection, not the earlier source. Formal68 = prior59 plus nine fresh component groups, all passing with no skips/failures/cancellations and29 source fingerprints stable. DOM fixtures exercise the real component and backend handle through actual button/keyboard handlers. Keyboard default Enter/Space button activation is explicitly simulated in the model; no real browser or assistive-technology result is claimed. Root browser acceptance and independent review remain pending.

Four candidate test files adapt prior UI harnesses. Successful operations explicitly click the new Confirm button; dirty rejection still invokes the original direct control and requires no confirmation. The common fixture exposes an explicit user-action helper and disposal/focus model, with no automatic decision. The two older UI bodies use that common fixture, replace native-dialog text expectations with visible scope assertions, and preserve cascade/cancel/restore/draft/held-duplicate requirements; its synthetic note title changes from Owned note to A note. Exact before/after source pairs, all baseline bodies and distinct epoch authority remain preserved. Backend tests and original helpers are unchanged. The replayed original helper corpus is finite historical comparison evidence, not a new held-out original campaign.

Two source-edit preparation errors and one failed finalization attempt are retained. The failed finalizer incorrectly expected three JSON native-dialog markers; two observation records write that field, while the third dirty-guard test asserts zero calls without writing it. Its exact collector source/error are saved; raw/test source are unchanged and no behavior rerun was required. No behavior test failure was observed. Both test children settled normally; the declared180-second child deadline and8MiB stdout/2MiB stderr retention bounds were not hit. Fingerprint I/O has no separate deadline, no hard memory watchdog exists and owned-root signaling is not atomic Windows descendant containment. No measurement, profiler, original GUI/full application or publication run occurred. The source-only public-map proposal excludes exact binary TAR/JEX fixture copies and keeps their hashes; no native original executable is copied.
